import LessonLayout from '../../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';
---
<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; The Seven Petitions" cic="CCC 2803-2865" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>What are the three petitions directed toward God and the four directed toward our needs?</li>
<li>What does "hallowing" God's name mean — making it holier or recognizing it as holy?</li>
<li>Why is the fifth petition ("forgive us our trespasses") the only one Jesus explicitly commented on after the Lord's Prayer?</li>
<li>What are the two meanings of "daily bread" according to the Church Fathers?</li>
<li>In the seventh petition, what evil are we primarily asking to be delivered from?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. Take your time.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. What person or situation do you still find hardest to forgive? Write their name (or initial) and what happened.</p>
<p class="question-block__p">This is not about justifying what happened, but acknowledging the wound. The first step toward forgiving is admitting that it hurts.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. Do you live anxiously worrying about the future or do you trust that God will provide your daily bread?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Think of something concrete that worries you (money, health, work, family). Have you surrendered it to God or are you carrying it alone?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. Of the first three petitions (Name, Kingdom, Will), which one is hardest for you to say with your heart? Why?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Is it hard to desire God's will? Are you afraid of what he might ask? Or is it hard to desire his Kingdom to come because you are comfortable in this world?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. In what area of your life do you feel you are "in temptation" right now? What concrete step can you take to resist it?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">The first step is to recognize it. The second is to ask for help. Who can you ask to pray for you in that struggle?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. Go through the seven petitions. Choose ONE you want to focus on this week. How are you going to live it?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">For example: if you choose "forgive us our trespasses," write down whom you are going to forgive or ask forgiveness from. If you choose "give us this day our daily bread," think of someone hungry whom you can help.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. Pray the Lord's Prayer Word by Word</h4>
<p>For an entire week, pray the Lord's Prayer JUST ONCE a day, but very slowly. Pause after each petition. With each one ask yourself: "Do I truly desire this?" Each day, write down which petition resonated most with you and why.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>B. Practice Forgiveness: A Concrete Act</h4>
<p>The fifth petition is the most demanding. This week, take a concrete step toward forgiveness. If there is someone you need to forgive: pray for that person for three days in a row. If you need to ask forgiveness: send a message or speak with that person. Do not put it off.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>C. Map of the Seven Petitions</h4>
<p>Draw a path with seven stations —like a Stations of the Cross but toward glory—. At each station write one of the seven petitions and draw something that represents it for you: a heart (Name), a castle (Kingdom), an open hand (Will), a loaf of bread (Bread), two clasped hands (Forgiveness), a shield (Temptation), a luminous cross (Deliver us from evil).</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Memory Verse</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p>&laquo;Our Father in heaven, hallowed be your name, your kingdom come, deliver us from evil.&raquo;</p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">&mdash; Matthew 6:9-10,13</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Prayer for This Week</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>Good Father,<br />
teach me to truly pray the Our Father.<br />
Let it not slip from my lips without passing through my heart.<br />
Let me truly desire your glory before my own.<br />
Let me truly trust in your daily bread,<br />
without fretting about tomorrow.<br />
Let me truly forgive those who have wounded me,<br />
as I want you to forgive me.<br />
Let me truly resist temptation,<br />
resting on your grace and not on my strength.<br />
And at the end, deliver me from evil<br />
and bring me home to you forever.<br />
Amen.</p>
</blockquote>

</section>

